          %title Environmental representation of quantum channels
          %h3#QuantumChannelsAndDecoherence Environmental representation of quantum channels
          %p
            The crux of dynamical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+decoherence"} quantum decoherence
            is that
            %em fundamentally
            the (time-)evolution of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
            may be assumed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+quantum+channel"} unitary
            (say via a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} Schrödinger equation
            %em when taking the whole evolution of its environment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{B}
            (the “bath”, ultimately the whole
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi.mathscript ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
            is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi evolve
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo |
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi β
                            %mo ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi tot
                          %mrow
                            %mo |
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi β
                            %mo ⟩
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathllap{
                  evolve
                  \\;\colon\;
                  }
                  \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
                  \\\
                  \\left\vert \psi, \beta \right\rangle
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  U_{tot}
                  \\left\vert \psi, \beta \right\rangle
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
                  }
          %p
            after understanding the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+states"} mixed states
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \,\colon\, \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{H}^\ast
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"}> density matrices
            ) of the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            as coupled to any given mixed state
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi env
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi.mathscript ℬ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi.mathscript ℬ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} env \,\colon\, \mathscr{B} \otimes \mathscr{B}^\ast
            of the bath (via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi couple
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi env
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathllap{
                  couple
                  \\;\colon\;
                  }
                  \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{H}^\ast
                  \&amp;
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \&amp;
                  (\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B})
                  \\otimes
                  (\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B})^\ast
                  \\\
                  \\rho &amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\rho \otimes env
                  \\mathrlap{\,;}
                  }
          %p
            …the only catch being that one cannot — and in any case does not (want or need to) — keep track of the precise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            of the environment/bath, instead only of its
            %em average
            effect on the given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability"} quantum probability
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+state"} mixed state
            that remains after the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+trace+quantum+channel"} partial trace
            over the environment:
          #eq:PartialTraceOverBathTowardsQuantumChannels.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi average
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi.mathscript ℬ
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ^
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Tr
                            %mi.mathscript ℬ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo ^
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathllap{
                  average
                  \\;\colon\;
                  }
                  (\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B})
                  \\otimes
                  (\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B})^\ast
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{H}^\ast
                  \\\
                  \\widehat{\rho}
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  Tr_{\mathscr{B}}\big(\widehat{\rho}\big)
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  }
          %p
            In summary this means
            %em for practical purposes
            that the probabilistic evolution of quantum systems
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
            is always of the composite form
          .maruku-equation
