          %p
            This composite turns out to be a “
            %em>
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+channel"} quantum channel
            ”
          %p
            The realization of a quantum channel in the form
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:QuantumChannelVieDecoherence"} (2)
            is also called an
            %em environmental representation
            (eg.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "quantum+channel#ŻyczkowskiBengtsson04"} Życzkowski &amp; Bengtsson 2004 (3.5)
          %p In fact all quantum channels on a fixed Hilbert space have such an evironmental representation:
          %p
          #QuantumChannelsAsPartialTracesOfUnitariesOnTensors.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (environmental representation of quantum channels)
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+channel"} quantum channel
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi chan
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    chan
                    \\;\;\colon\;\;
                    \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{H}^\ast
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{H}^\ast
            %p may be written as
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+quantum+channel"} unitary quantum channel
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi tot
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi.mathscript ℬ
                        %mo →
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi.mathscript ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{tot} \,\colon\, \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B} \to \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
              %li
                %p
                  on a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compound+system"} compound system
                  with some
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{B}
                  (the “bath”), yielding a
                  %em total system
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi.mathscript ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \otimes \mathscr{B}
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+Hilbert+spaces"}> tensor product
                  ),
              %li
                %p
                  and acting on the given
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+state"} mixed state
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  coupled (tensored) with any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"} pure state
                  of the bath system,
              %li
                %p
                  followed by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+trace+quantum+channel"} partial trace
                  (averaging) over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{B}
                  (leading to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decoherence"} decoherence
                  in the remaining state)
            %p in that
            #eq:QuantumChannelVieDecoherence.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi chan
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Tr
                      %mi.mathscript ℬ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi tot
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi env
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
